--------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------

This project stands on work done by others. Where possible we embed or
depend on their code rather than reimplementing it — that is a
deliberate design choice, not a shortcut.

adblock-rust — Mozilla Public License 2.0
  https://github.com/brave/adblock-rust
  Brave's content blocking engine. Embedded to provide ad, tracker and
  cosmetic filtering. We do not implement our own blocking engine.

Tauri — Apache License 2.0 / MIT
  https://github.com/tauri-apps/tauri
  Application shell across desktop and mobile, running on each
  platform's own webview.

TensorFlow.js — Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/tensorflow/tfjs
  On-device inference runtime (tfjs-core, tfjs-converter, and the CPU
  and WebGL backends) powering the gaze protection module.

BlazeFace model — Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/tensorflow/tfjs-models (Google / MediaPipe)
  Face-presence detection model, embedded (base64) in the gaze
  module's bundle so no network fetch is ever needed.

nsfwjs — MIT License
  https://github.com/infinitered/nsfwjs
  On-device NSFW classification; the MobileNetV2 model files shipped
  in the nsfwjs package are embedded the same way as BlazeFace.

dsojevic/profanity-list — MIT License
  https://github.com/dsojevic/profanity-list
  Seed keyword list for the protection engine's text signals. A
  snapshot lives at app/gaze/vendor/profanity-en.json; only the
  sexual/shock-tagged entries are embedded in the gaze bundle.

obscenity — MIT License
  https://github.com/jo3-l/obscenity
  Text-matching engine (evasion normalization: leetspeak, confusables,
  repeated characters) used by the protection engine's text signals.

vladmandic/human and human-models — MIT License
  https://github.com/vladmandic/human
  The gaze module's BlazeFace box decode + anchor generation are
  adapted from Human's implementation (see app/gaze/src/detector.js),
  and the gender classifier (SSR-Net architecture) is the converted
  model distributed in vladmandic/human-models, embedded (base64) like
  the other models.

EasyList / EasyPrivacy — dual-licensed GPLv3 / CC BY-SA 3.0
  https://easylist.to/
  Consumed as upstream filter data by the embedded engine. Snapshots
  live under rules/vendor/ and keep their own licences (they are NOT
  covered by rules/'s CC0 dedication).

uBlock Origin filter lists — GNU GPLv3
  https://github.com/uBlockOrigin/uAssets
  Same treatment: vendored data snapshots under rules/vendor/, their
  licence intact.

Brave adblock resources (resources.json) — Mozilla Public License 2.0
  https://github.com/brave/adblock-resources
  Scriptlet/redirect resource definitions consumed by the engine.

